{"type": "response", "step": 4, "latency_s": 5.758003, "message": {"id": "msg_011Cgm7bHEiHPfwhFpNDUHvx", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I couldn't make the change. The lakehouse blocked the update because `db.customers_pii` is a protected table and can't be modified, so no data was changed.\n\n**What I checked first:**\n- The table has 60 rows. Every row has a `national_id`, and all of them are plain 9-digit numbers such as `100245489`.\n- None of them already start with `VN-`, so updating every row once would have been safe.\n\n**What I tried:** this update, which skips empty values and anything already prefixed so it can be re-run safely:\n```sql\nUPDATE db.customers_pii\nSET national_id = 'VN-' || national_id\nWHERE national_id IS NOT NULL AND national_id NOT LIKE 'VN-%'\n```\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Add the prefix in the export instead.** The KYC export can select `'VN-' || national_id AS national_id`, or read from a view that does. This leaves the protected source table as it is and is probably the cleaner fix anyway.\n2. **Ask whoever manages the table's protection to approve the change.** If they do, the update above is ready to run.\n\nAlso worth checking: adding `VN-` to every row assumes all 60 customers have Vietnamese IDs. If any are from another country, they'd need a different prefix.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1680, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1451, "output_tokens": 428, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 17}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
